        "instruction": "Turn the ring in diagram direction b to increase preload or c to decrease it. Allowed shortening from measured free length is 1.5–18.0 mm; stock reference is 10.0 mm. One ring turn changes installed length 1.5 mm. Choose a measured setting within those bounds to approach 90–100 mm rider sag, then tighten the locknut as Yamaha directs; this section gives no numeric locknut torque. If rider sag is above 100 mm, increase preload; below 90 mm, decrease preload. Keep the measured preload within its limits.",
