        "title": "Remove piston and rings",
        "instruction": "Cover the crankcase opening before removing a piston-pin clip. Deburr the clip groove and pin-bore area as required; withdraw the pin without hammering. If still difficult, use piston-pin puller 90890-01304 / YU-01304. Remove the piston, then top ring and oil-ring components by opening the ring ends carefully and lifting the opposite side over the crown. Account for clips and protect the exposed connecting rod and crankcase.",
