        "title": "Measure journal clearance",
        "instruction": "Temporarily place each cam in its original head position. Lay Plastigauge on the illustrated journal, install original dowels and caps, and tighten cap bolts to 10 N·m in a crisscross pattern from inside outward; the illustrated bolts use engine oil on threads/contact surfaces. Do not rotate the cam during measurement. Remove caps evenly and measure the strip width. Record clearance against 0.028–0.062 mm. Remove all Plastigauge residue afterward.",
