        "instruction": "Use the exact six-position removal diagram: loosen each head fastener half a turn per pass in the illustrated order until all are fully loose, then remove. Keep the long M9×145 mm bolt at position3 distinct from the three M9×135 mm bolts at positions4–6. Lift the head while retaining the timing chain; remove the old gasket and intake-side chain guide. Retain dowels and washers. Leave oil-passage plug and head studs installed.",
