        "title": "Check the head and guide",
        "instruction": "Inspect the intake-side chain guide for damage/wear. Remove combustion-chamber carbon with a rounded scraper without scratching the plug bore or head. Clear coolant-passage deposits/rust. Record head damage and check warpage with straightedge and thickness gauge across the illustrated paths; limit 0.05 mm. Head replacement also requires new valves. A failed warpage check needs a separately reviewed resurfacing operation; do not count this inspection as machining.",
