        "instruction": "Clean carbon from grooves/rings. Record top and second-ring side clearances: each standard 0.030–0.065 mm, limit 0.100 mm. Out-of-specification side clearance requires the piston and rings as a set. For each end-gap check, square the ring near the bottom of the cylinder using the piston crown, as illustrated, where wear is lowest. Measure and record the end gap; each limit is 0.95 mm. Replace an out-of-specification ring. The cited source does not state a new-ring minimum end gap; do not file rings to an invented target.",
