        "title": "Right fork: fit the rod, washer and adjuster",
        "instruction": "Record and fully loosen the rebound control. Compress the inner tube and position the ring wrench under the locknut as illustrated. Fit the damper adjusting rod, new copper washer and adjuster. Finger-tighten the adjuster fully onto the damper rod. Before torquing, measure the gap between adjuster and locknut: it must be 0.5–1.0 mm. Correct the locknut/adjuster position if outside that range.",
