        "instruction": "Index all twelve case bolts: five 45 mm, four 60 mm and three 75 mm at their exact map positions. Loosen each a quarter-turn at a time before removing them. Lay the engine left side down. Use only the designated splitting slit for a screwdriver tip, with light soft-hammer taps on reinforced splitting or mounting bosses. Lift the right case evenly, leaving crank and gearbox in the left. If separation resists, find the remaining bolt or fitting; do not force or strike a gasket surface. Collect dowels and any O-ring encountered.",
