        "title": "Release and lift the head",
        "instruction": "Use the removal diagram on this page, which is different from the tightening numbering. Loosen each bolt half a turn per pass in illustrated order 1–6 until all are loose, then remove them. The two small bolts are M6×35 mm and four main bolts M10×149 mm. Lift the head, retain dowels and intake-side chain guide, and remove the head gasket while keeping the chain supported. Leave head studs and oil-passage plugs installed.",
