        "id": "topend-cam-disposition",
        "title": "Resolve cam and chain defects",
        "instruction": "If journal clearance failed, measure journal OD against 21.959–21.972 mm: a failed journal requires a cam, while an in-range journal with failed clearance requires head and caps together. Inspect chain for stiffness/damage and sprockets for more than one-quarter tooth wear; either condition requires chain and cam replacement as a set. Check smooth decompressor movement and projecting lever pin. Cross-check the recorded lower-chain inspection and installed crank/chain against the cams selected here. Any required matched crank-sprocket, chain and cam set must now be complete and individually accepted; do not retain old cams when matched renewal is required. Head/cap-set replacement remains outside this route.",
