        "instruction": "New valves, piston, rings, camshaft or gears require about 30 minutes at no more than half throttle. A new cylinder or crankshaft requires about one hour: 20 minutes at no more than half throttle, inspect, then 40 minutes at no more than three-quarter throttle and inspect again. With both groups renewed, keep at or below half throttle for the first 30 minutes; this overlap is an explicit conservative workflow adaptation. Record the actual parts route.",
