        "instruction": "Reconnect stator, crankshaft-position, gear-position and coolant-temperature connectors and their covers. Route stator lead behind the radiator, clear of the tension arm and gear-position connector. The clutch cable protector contacts the radiator hose and passes outside the stator and gear leads. Fasten clutch cable, gear lead and stator lead over the grommet with the tie end forward and cut off excess. Clamp the clutch cable ahead of the leads, seat the frame clip with its lock forward and trim excess as illustrated. Keep regulator leads inside the tension arm. Fully seat the plug cap and route temperature, engine-ground and high-tension leads outside the head breather. Check the starter lead stays clear of the push lever shaft.",
        "source_pdf_pages": [
          62,
          63,
          66,
          67,
          70,
          71
        ],
        "verification": [
          "Every labeled connector latched/covered; source routing and tie locations verified."
        ],
