        "id": "commission-chain",
        "title": "Set chain alignment and slack",
        "instruction": "With the rear wheel raised and transmission neutral, pull up the chain about 50 N above the guide mounting bolt and measure the illustrated guide-to-chain gap: 50–60 mm. To adjust, loosen axle nut and both locknuts; adjust sides equally and push wheel forward to seat both end plates. Tighten axle 135 N·m and locknuts 21 N·m, then recheck alignment/slack. Lubricate the chain. A stiff, damaged or worn chain requires separate cleaning/removal or replacement and clip closure; do not hide that work behind this inspection.",
