        "title": "Resolve cam and chain defects",
        "instruction": "If journal clearance failed, measure journal OD against 22.002–22.015 mm: a failed journal requires a cam, while an in-range journal with failed clearance requires head and caps together. Inspect chain for stiffness/damage and sprockets for more than one-quarter tooth wear; either condition requires chain and cam replacement as a set. Check smooth decompressor movement and projecting lever pin. Cross-check the recorded lower-chain inspection and installed crank/chain against the cams selected here. Any required matched crank-sprocket/chain/cam set must now be complete and individually accepted; do not retain old cams when matched-set renewal is required. The head/cap-set replacement remains outside this route.",
