        "id": "commission-controls",
        "title": "Inspect and lubricate controls",
        "instruction": "Check both brakes for effective action without drag and the front-lever end for no free play. With reservoirs horizontal, fluid must be above the minimum marks in the diagram. Leaks or spongy action require separate brake service. Check cable-clutch free play at 7.0–12.0 mm: turn the handlebar adjuster; if insufficient, slide the cable cover, loosen its locknut, adjust at the cable, tighten that locknut to 4.3 N·m and restore the cover. Check smooth clutch action and unrestricted cable travel through full steering. Replace damaged cables; lubricate rough sound cables with engine oil or suitable cable lubricant at the upright cable end. Use silicone grease at brake-lever moving contacts and lithium-soap grease at clutch-lever and pedal pivots.",
