        "title": "Seat the forks before final axle tightening",
        "instruction": "With the bike securely supported on its wheels, push down on the handlebars several times and confirm smooth fork rebound before final axle-nut tightening, as Yamaha specifies. Tighten the axle nut to 115 N·m, then all four axle pinch bolts to 21 N·m. This is a stationary seating operation, not permission to ride with loose axle hardware.",
