        "id": "front-steering-close",
        "title": "Verify steering and front-end closure",
        "instruction": "Check the rebuilt steering and front end now: no play or binding, smooth fork action, wheel correctly secured and firm front brake. Inspect hose/cable clearance while the remaining assemblies are still supported. Repeat whole-bike checks after the remaining fluid and startup checks are complete. With the refitted front wheel supported clear on its final-torqued axle, verify smooth rotation without bearing play. Use a stable dial gauge at the PDF124 rim locations; record radial and lateral runout, each no more than 2.0 mm. Correct any binding or out-of-limit wheel before use.",
