        "instruction": "Remove the coolant drain bolt and its copper washer. Place a thick cloth over the radiator cap and turn it slowly counterclockwise toward its detent to release residual pressure. Once hissing stops, press down and turn farther to remove the cap. Let the coolant drain into the container. Thoroughly flush the cooling system with clean tap water as Yamaha directs, then drain the flush water completely before fitting the new drain washer. Account for residual water when establishing the final coolant mixture.",
