        "id": "loom-control-off",
        "title": "Lift the supported controls and main harness clear",
        "instruction": "The throttle grip is off the bar and its cable ends are detached; keep the identified cables attached to the intact throttle body and independently supported. Release remaining frame/cable holders and ties using the exact routing diagrams. Unbolt rectifier/regulator, ignition-coil bracket and air-filter-case brackets, retaining connectors where possible. Before independently lifting the throttle-body group clear of the loom, label and disconnect the intake-pressure sensor dark-blue 3-pin, injector gray 2-pin and throttle-position sensor black 3-pin couplers by their latches. Keep the sensors installed and protect connector halves; never pull on the wires. Lift the harness and supported bar with its closed front-brake assembly and cable clutch clear; lift the separate throttle-body/cable group clear without kinking. No hose or cable bears another component's weight. Closed hydraulic lines remain attached to their supported controls; modified routing preventing this removal is outside this route. Identify and disconnect the frame ground terminal so it does not tether the loom; retain its bolt and photograph its position.",
