        "id": "tank-cleaning-record",
        "title": "Record the required tank-interior service",
        "instruction": "The post-break-in list requires cleaning inside the fuel tank and checking for leaks. Record actual qualified cleaning, not merely an appointment or fuel-color inspection. The cleaning method remains an external dependency. Follow exact tank access/refit: extract fuel with a pump; remove seat, side covers and shrouds; cover residual-pressure fittings with cloth, release holder/cover and both connector buttons by hand, protect disconnected joints and support the tank off its pump face. If pump removed, renew gasket lip upward, align pump projection with bracket slot and tighten the five bolts in the numbered order to 7 N·m. Restore tank front bolts 8 N·m and retaining screw 4 N·m, reconnect fuel hose until it clicks, restore connector cover and correctly oriented holder, and connect pump coupler. Record restored sealing and leak checks.",
