        "id": "engine-in--final-checks",
        "title": "Verify the installed engine and record closure",
        "instruction": "Follow the oil-level procedure with the bike upright: warm oil to normal operating temperature, run for 10 seconds, stop and allow a few minutes to settle; level must be between window minimum and maximum mark. Check leaks, normal clutch/brake operation, throttle free play 3–6 mm and full return; turn the bars both ways and verify idle does not change. Record all mount torques, fluid quantities, chain slack and unresolved symptoms. Save the accepted top-end measurements with these installation checks. This records only the work actually performed; bottom-end work is not included. Seat refacing is recorded as the external operation actually completed. The bike is assembled and stationary checks are complete; new-valve run-in and its follow-up maintenance remain required. With correctly configured YDT 90890-03275 (US USB) or 90890-03273, verify coolant at 70–80 °C. Use tachometer 90890-06760 or YU-39951-B connected as shown to the ignition-coil high-tension lead to verify 1900–2100 r/min with starter knob fully returned and serviceable filter/compression/free play. Adjust idle if necessary; clockwise raises speed. Record actual temperature and idle, then repeat the steering/return check.",
