        "instruction": "Inspect the tensioner for cracks or damage. While lightly pressing the rod with a finger, turn its screw fully clockwise with a thin screwdriver to retract it. Release the screwdriver while maintaining light finger pressure and verify that the rod extends smoothly. Replace a damaged or sticking unit; do not install one that fails this check.",
